    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Kyle Tucker** (80.24), who both benefit immensely from favorable park conditions and porous matchups against Walker Buehler and Erick Fedde, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** stands out as the premier play due to a synergy of high-leverage order placement, a 16% park boost, and a projected wind-out scenario at the stadium. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** is in a prime position to capitalize on Fedde\u2019s projected struggles; his 80.24 score is driven by an elite SP skill advantage that suggests he will see high-quality pitches in advantageous counts. **Andy Pages** (74.02) and **Jackson Merrill** (71.85) also provide high-efficiency scoring, with **Jackson Merrill** specifically benefiting from a subtle boost related to the pitcher's delivery tempo, which historically creates stolen base opportunities\u2014a critical component of our team\u2019s scarcity management strategy.\n\nThe most difficult decision for today's roster involved **Nolan Schanuel** (52.28), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Wade Meckler** (49.40) and **Sam Antonacci** (48.42). While **Nolan Schanuel** technically carried a higher raw projection than our final outfielder selections, the optimizer prioritized the specific platoon advantages and higher batting order slots afforded to **Wade Meckler** and **Sam Antonacci**. Despite the benching of **Nolan Schanuel** and **Josh Jung** (51.61), we remain wary of the risk surrounding **Liam Hicks** (42.69); he faces Paul Skenes, whose 2.99 xERA creates a significant \"SP Skill\" drag on his production. While **Liam Hicks** earns his spot based on the projected leadoff role, he sits firmly in our \"marginal\" tier today; we will be monitoring the official lineup cards closely to ensure none of our starters are pushed into unfavorable defensive positions or defensive replacements due to these challenging SP matchups.",
